    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **62 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (which handles `POST /api/owners`).\n\nThe `Idempotency-Key` header isn't part of the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` signature, so I read it from the current request via a constructor-injected `HttpServletRequest` (Spring's standard request-scoped proxy) rather than altering the generated contract.\n\nChanges in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> idempotentCreates` mapping a seen key \u2192 the created owner's id, plus the `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_HEADER` constant and the `HttpServletRequest` dependency.\n- At the **start** of `addOwner`: if the request carries a non-blank `Idempotency-Key` that's already been recorded, it fetches that original owner and returns it with **200 OK**, short-circuiting all validation/duplicate logic (which would otherwise 409).\n- After a successful `saveOwner`: if a key was supplied, it records `key \u2192 owner.id` so subsequent repeats resolve to the same owner.\n\nNew owners still return **201 Created** as before; only a repeat with an already-seen key returns 200 with the original owner. `Cp50Tests` and all 62 tests pass.",
