    "probe_text": "POST `/api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:611`), which delegates final persistence to `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`. Here is everything that happens, in execution order. I mark each step as **[validation]** (can reject the request) or **[side-effect]** (mutates state / the response).\n\n## In `addOwner`\n\n1. **[validation] Authorization** (`@PreAuthorize`, line 611) \u2014 caller must hold role `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n2. **[side-effect] Idempotency short-circuit** (lines 614\u2013623) \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If it was seen before *and* the owner it created still exists, the original owner is returned with `200 OK` and none of the steps below run.\n\n3. **[side-effect] Address normalization** (`applyAddressFields`, line 624) \u2014 mutates the DTO. If `addressLine1` is present, the structured lines are trimmed/whitespace-collapsed/upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`), and the flat `address` is recomposed from them; otherwise the flat `address` alone is normalized. (Runs *before* the required-field check, so the composed `address` can satisfy it.)\n\n4. **[validation] Required fields** (`validateRequiredFields`, line 625) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank, else `RequiredFieldsMissingException` listing each missing field.\n\n5. **[validation] Postcode** (`validatePostcode`, line 626) \u2014 optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits and fall within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown city accepts any 4-digit code. Else `InvalidFieldsException(\"postcode\")`.\n\n6. **[validation + side-effect] Telephone normalization** (`normalizeTelephone`, line 627) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, applies `+61` default (dropping a leading `0`), requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, and enforces fixed national length (AU `61`\u21929 digits, NANP `1`\u219210). Else `InvalidFieldsException(\"telephone\")`. Produces the E.164 value.\n\n7. **[validation] City capacity** (`requireCityHasCapacity`, line 628) \u2014 rejects if the city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n8. **[validation + side-effect] Email normalization** (`normalizeEmail`, line 629) \u2014 optional; blank \u2192 `null`. If present, must match the syntactic email pattern and its domain must not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), else `InvalidFieldsException(\"email\")`. Returns the lower-cased address.\n\n9. **[side-effect] Map to entity** (lines 631\u2013634) \u2014 DTO \u2192 `Owner`, then sets the normalized `telephone`, normalized `email`, and `deleted = false`.\n\n10. **[validation] Unique identity** (`requireUniqueIdentity`, line 635) \u2014 rejects if any non-deleted owner already has the same normalized telephone \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`. (Despite the \"identity key\" naming, the actual collision test is on telephone only.)\n\n11. **[validation] Household duplicate** (`requireNoHouseholdDuplicate`, lines 636\u2013639) \u2014 skipped when the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`. Otherwise, if the owner has a postcode and its household id (SHA-256 of normalized lastName + postcode) matches a non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`.\n\n12. **[validation] Registration date not in future** (`requireRegistrationDateNotInFuture`, line 640) \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` after today (2026-08-11) \u2192 `InvalidFieldsException(\"registrationDate\")`. `null` is allowed.\n\n13. **[side-effect] Business-day adjustment** (lines 641\u2013644) \u2014 effective date = supplied date or today; then rolled forward past weekends and listed public holidays to the next business day, and stored on the owner.\n\n14. **[validation] Daily limit** (`requireDailyLimitNotReached`, line 645) \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already share that (adjusted) registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n15. **[side-effect] Bulk-signup flag** (`isBulkSignup`, line 646) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 owners already share that date (create still succeeds).\n\n16. **[side-effect] Possible-duplicate flags** (`findPossibleDuplicate`, lines 647\u2013649) \u2014 skipped when `sharesHousehold=true`. Otherwise finds the lowest-id non-deleted owner with the same last name + postcode but a *different* telephone, and sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\n17. **[side-effect] Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`, line 650) \u2014 see below.\n\n18. **[side-effect] Record idempotency key** (lines 651\u2013653) \u2014 maps the `Idempotency-Key` to the new owner's id.\n\n19. **[side-effect] Audit log** (lines 654\u2013656) \u2014 writes one line to the `AUDIT` logger with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n20. **[side-effect] Response** (lines 657\u2013660) \u2014 builds the `OwnerDto` (which derives all the computed fields: salutation, displayName, initials, householdId, identityKey, membership number/level/points, locality, timezone, etc.), sets the `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, and returns `201 CREATED`.\n\n## Inside `saveOwner` (step 17, `ClinicServiceImpl.java:237`)\n\nOnly for a new owner, and each only if not already set:\n\n17a. **[side-effect] Customer code** (`generateCustomerCode`) \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region derived from postcode (fallback city), hash from telephone + last name, then de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix against existing codes.\n\n17b. **[side-effect] Namesake count** \u2014 count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n17c. **[side-effect] Household member count** \u2014 count of existing owners sharing normalized last name + postcode, plus one (the new owner).\n\n17d. **[side-effect] Repository save** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`, assigning the id.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the \"identity key\" uniqueness check (step 10) actually only compares telephone, not the full `telephone|email|householdId` key its docs describe; and Bean Validation constraints on the entity (`@NotEmpty` address/city/telephone, the E.164 `@Pattern`) exist but the controller's own normalization/validation runs first, so they act as a backstop at persist time."
